00:49:55,186 --> 00:49:58,080
- [Mike] Well, he's crusty
but extremely unlikable.

1501
00:49:58,080 --> 00:50:00,023
- Mostly crusty.

1502
00:50:00,023 --> 00:50:03,559
Hey, they strapped the
general onto that one.

1503
00:50:03,559 --> 00:50:06,892
- [Servo] Ooh, at least excuse yourself.

1504
00:50:09,827 --> 00:50:12,872
- [Mike] Uh-oh, that
wasn't supposed to happen.

1505
00:50:12,872 --> 00:50:16,955
(suspenseful instrumental music)

1506
00:50:18,284 --> 00:50:19,884
- [Servo] Uh-huh.

1507
00:50:19,884 --> 00:50:21,541
- [Mike] Right.

1508
00:50:21,541 --> 00:50:23,970
- Wow, they've taken
Jarts to the next level.

1509
00:50:23,970 --> 00:50:26,220
(laughing)

1510
00:50:28,449 --> 00:50:30,005
- [Mike] Aw, the plane is pregnant.

1511
00:50:30,005 --> 00:50:32,338
(baby talk)

1512
00:50:37,563 --> 00:50:41,646
- [Servo] Geez, up or
down, you kids, up or down!

1513
00:50:44,118 --> 00:50:45,129
- [Mike] Ah yes.

1514
00:50:45,129 --> 00:50:47,309
- Ah, the association are back.

1515
00:50:47,309 --> 00:50:48,142
Is, are.

1516
00:50:49,497 --> 00:50:50,330
Was.

1517
00:50:50,330 --> 00:50:51,163
- [Servo] Whatever.

1518
00:50:51,163 --> 00:50:53,927
- [Mike] Steve, your head looks
like an egg from back here.

1519
00:50:53,927 --> 00:50:55,770
- [Servo] I suppose their last project

1520
00:50:55,770 --> 00:50:59,103
before The Ray Conniff Singers broke up.

1521
00:51:02,055 --> 00:51:03,039
This is high enough for me,

1522
00:51:03,039 --> 00:51:04,706
thank you very much.

1523
00:51:07,001 --> 00:51:11,434
- [Mike] (humming) It's catchy.

1524
00:51:11,434 --> 00:51:12,572
- [Servo] Oh, Pueblo tapestry,

1525
00:51:12,572 --> 00:51:15,072
let's blow the hell out of it!

1526
00:51:16,092 --> 00:51:18,230
- This is still better than Iron Eagle.

1527
00:51:18,230 --> 00:51:19,796
- [Servo] Cha-cha-cha. (mimics static)

1528
00:51:19,796 --> 00:51:21,784
- [Voiceover] Cordite lead, Cordite two.

1529
00:51:21,784 --> 00:51:23,629
- [Mike] Cordite two, you're on the air.

1530
00:51:23,629 --> 00:51:24,919
What do you think of the
Clinton Administration?

1531
00:51:24,919 --> 00:51:25,883
- [Voiceover] Go ahead, two.

1532
00:51:25,883 --> 00:51:26,963
- [Voiceover] Lead,
I've got troubles here.

1533
00:51:26,963 --> 00:51:29,139
My number two hydraulic
system is dropping rapidly.

1534
00:51:29,139 --> 00:51:29,972
- [Servo] Hmm.

1535
00:51:29,972 --> 00:51:31,135
- [Voiceover] All right,
let's clear the range,

1536
00:51:31,135 --> 00:51:32,036
and I'll get on your wing.

1537
00:51:32,036 --> 00:51:33,404
Pick up a heading for the base.

1538
00:51:33,404 --> 00:51:35,321
- [Voiceover] Yes, sir.

1539
00:51:37,597 --> 00:51:39,261
- [Servo] Well, you can tell
it's a dangerous situation

1540
00:51:39,261 --> 00:51:41,181
by the music, tell 'em.

1541
00:51:41,181 --> 00:51:42,014
- Yes.

1542
00:51:44,030 --> 00:51:45,803
- [Voiceover] Cordite two, any change yet?

1543
00:51:45,803 --> 00:51:48,202
- [Voiceover] Negative, gauge
says there's nothing left.

1544
00:51:48,202 --> 00:51:49,302
- [Voiceover] Okay, lower your airspeed

1545
00:51:49,302 --> 00:51:51,969
to 120 knots and drop your gear.

1546
00:51:52,856 --> 00:51:54,539
- Ah, it's a spare.

1547
00:51:54,539 --> 00:51:58,206
Good only for 10 miles
at 50 miles per hour.

1548
00:51:59,137 --> 00:52:01,828
- [Voiceover] Your gear looks
okay, are you indicating more?

1549
00:52:01,828 --> 00:52:03,765
- [Voiceover] No sir, I've
got an unsafe gear indication,

1550
00:52:03,765 --> 00:52:06,519
and my number two hydraulic
system reads absolute zero.

1551
00:52:06,519 --> 00:52:07,876
- [Mike] What is right with you?

1552
00:52:07,876 --> 00:52:09,984
- [Voiceover] Just run your
manual emergency gear release.

1553
00:52:09,984 --> 00:52:14,067
- [Servo] Oh, and my tape
deck won't work either.

1554
00:52:16,188 --> 00:52:18,606
- [Voiceover] Cordite lead,
still reading unsafe here.

1555
00:52:18,606 --> 00:52:20,170
- [Servo] Hmm.

1556
00:52:20,170 --> 00:52:21,083
- [Voiceover] Hold, Cordite.

1557
00:52:21,083 --> 00:52:23,222
Calling and requesting emergency
for straight in approach.

1558
00:52:23,222 --> 00:52:25,353
- Uh, go ahead and kiss your ass goodbye.

1559
00:52:25,353 --> 00:52:27,037
- [Voiceover] George tower, Cordite lead.

1560
00:52:27,037 --> 00:52:28,253
- [Mike] I'm incapable of love, over.

1561
00:52:28,253 --> 00:52:29,706
- Cordite lead, George tower over.

1562
00:52:29,706 --> 00:52:30,769
- [Voiceover] George, Cordite lead.

1563
00:52:30,769 --> 00:52:32,623
Request emergency landing for 104.

1564
00:52:32,623 --> 00:52:33,742
- [Mike] That's trash, oh.

1565
00:52:33,742 --> 00:52:35,279
- [Voiceover] Approximately
30 miles north.

1566
00:52:35,279 --> 00:52:36,703
Request straight in approach.

1567
00:52:36,703 --> 00:52:38,829
My wingman has a
hydraulic utility failure.

1568
00:52:38,829 --> 00:52:40,681
Landing gear down but indicating unsafe.

1569
00:52:40,681 --> 00:52:41,886
I'm declaring emergency.

1570
00:52:41,886 --> 00:52:42,951
- [Servo] And he's crying too.

1571
00:52:42,951 --> 00:52:44,984
- Roger, Cordite lead, we'll
clear the pattern for you

1572
00:52:44,984 --> 00:52:47,466
to land on runway one
six straight in approach.

1573
00:52:47,466 --> 00:52:50,066
- [Voiceover] Cordite check.

1574
00:52:50,066 --> 00:52:51,481
- Emergency, emergency.

1575
00:52:51,481 --> 00:52:53,036
F-104 hydraulic failure.

1576
00:52:53,036 --> 00:52:55,869
Landing from straight in
approach runway one six.

1577
00:52:55,869 --> 00:52:59,112
- Oh cheeks, we gotta save baby pants.

1578
00:52:59,112 --> 00:53:00,691
(suspenseful music)

1579
00:53:00,691 --> 00:53:02,213
- [Servo] It sounds like
a Russian national anthem.

1580
00:53:02,213 --> 00:53:04,517
- [Mike] Yeah, they would.

1581
00:53:04,517 --> 00:53:07,545
- The turtle called Gabra
is approaching the base.

1582
00:53:07,545 --> 00:53:09,069
- [Servo] Whoa.

1583
00:53:09,069 --> 00:53:10,414
- [Mike] The hippies got those

1584
00:53:10,414 --> 00:53:11,619
when they were done with them.

1585
00:53:11,619 --> 00:53:14,022
(laughs)

1586
00:53:14,022 --> 00:53:18,489
- A giant hippity hop
is called into action.

1587
00:53:18,489 --> 00:53:20,961
- Attention all aircraft,
vicinity George Air Force Base.

1588
00:53:20,961 --> 00:53:22,356
We have an emergency landing.

1589
00:53:22,356 --> 00:53:24,240
Be clear of George traffic pattern.

1590
00:53:24,240 --> 00:53:25,789
I repeat, we have an emergency.

1591
00:53:25,789 --> 00:53:27,968
Maintain radio silence.

1592
00:53:27,968 --> 00:53:29,764
- [Servo] All this because
a girl wouldn't kiss him.

1593
00:53:29,764 --> 00:53:31,006
- [Voiceover] Cordite two, any change yet?

1594
00:53:31,006 --> 00:53:32,901
- [Voiceover] Negative,
lead, same indications here.

1595
00:53:32,901 --> 00:53:35,327
- [Voiceover] Junior, prepare
that sweat that bird down.

1596
00:53:35,327 --> 00:53:36,946
- [Voiceover] I think
I can handle it, major.

1597
00:53:36,946 --> 00:53:39,318
I just hope this gear doesn't
fold up when I touch down.

1598
00:53:39,318 --> 00:53:40,151
- [Servo] Mm-hmm.

1599
00:53:40,151 --> 00:53:41,717
- [Mike] (singing) We
got a great big convoy,

1600
00:53:41,717 --> 00:53:43,967
truckin' through the night.

1601
00:53:44,824 --> 00:53:47,603
- Oops, uh, sorry, it's just
my seatbelt's in the door.

1602
00:53:47,603 --> 00:53:48,436
- [Servo] Doh.

1603
00:53:48,436 --> 00:53:50,099
- [Voiceover] John, from here,
all three wheels are down

1604
00:53:50,099 --> 00:53:51,350
and appear to be locked tight.

1605
00:53:51,350 --> 00:53:52,848
- [Voiceover] Rog.

1606
00:53:52,848 --> 00:53:54,351
- [Mike] Hi Dwayne, what's happening?

1607
00:53:54,351 --> 00:53:55,257
- [Voiceover] Stay with you, I want you to

1608
00:53:55,257 --> 00:53:56,956
make a normal approach in landing.

1609
00:53:56,956 --> 00:53:58,938
Emergency equipment is standing by.

1610
00:53:58,938 --> 00:53:59,771
- [Servo] (mimics static) Captain,

1611
00:53:59,771 --> 00:54:01,000
we're out of Colombia coffee.

1612
00:54:01,000 --> 00:54:04,414
(suspenseful music)

1613
00:54:04,414 --> 00:54:06,965
- I know I'm supposed to
feel something, but I don't.

1614
00:54:06,965 --> 00:54:09,084
- [Servo] Mm-mm, I'm with you.

1615
00:54:09,084 --> 00:54:10,139
- [Voiceover] George tower, Cordite lead.

1616
00:54:10,139 --> 00:54:12,281
We're five miles out on final.

1617
00:54:12,281 --> 00:54:13,804
- Cordite lead, George tower, roger.

1618
00:54:13,804 --> 00:54:15,169
Traffic is clear for you to land.

1619
00:54:15,169 --> 00:54:17,701
- [Servo] I'm going on break.

1620
00:54:17,701 --> 00:54:19,982
- [Mike] (singing) dum-dee-dum-dum.

1621
00:54:19,982 --> 00:54:23,017
- This guy gets wigged out
if his floor mats are uneven.

1622
00:54:23,017 --> 00:54:26,236
(suspenseful music)

1623
00:54:26,236 --> 00:54:30,551
- [Servo] Did they ever consider
that this wasn't riveting?

1624
00:54:30,551 --> 00:54:32,606
- [Mike] Boy, the potential
for something to happen

1625
00:54:32,606 --> 00:54:35,346
is very high right now.

1626
00:54:35,346 --> 00:54:38,014
- You know, it's a, this is
about a lot more than flying.

1627
00:54:38,014 --> 00:54:40,827
- [Mike] Yeah, yeah,
it's about landing too.

1628
00:54:40,827 --> 00:54:44,029
- [Servo] Oh no not runway
two, we just seal coated it.

1629
00:54:44,029 --> 00:54:47,287
(suspenseful music)

1630
00:54:47,287 --> 00:54:51,287
- Whoo, I bet he feels a
little silly right now.

1631
00:54:52,124 --> 00:54:53,476
- [Mike] Well, that's the moron's problem,

1632
00:54:53,476 --> 00:54:55,755
he's got parachutes jammed in his plane.

1633
00:54:55,755 --> 00:54:56,588
- [Servo] Oh no wonder.

1634
00:54:56,588 --> 00:54:58,571
- Here come the three stooges.

1635
00:54:58,571 --> 00:55:01,440
(hums tune)

1636
00:55:01,440 --> 00:55:02,860
- [Voiceover] See, John, no sweat.

1637
00:55:02,860 --> 00:55:04,708
Let the fire department
put the gear pins in,

1638
00:55:04,708 --> 00:55:06,092
and they'll throw the bird back.

1639
00:55:06,092 --> 00:55:07,957
- [Mike] Read some of the gauges wrong.

1640
00:55:07,957 --> 00:55:10,548
It's different than the other plane.

1641
00:55:10,548 --> 00:55:12,626
- This movie just faced us.

1642
00:55:12,626 --> 00:55:16,022
- [Servo] Ah, one of the
great anticlimaxes, huh?

1643
00:55:16,022 --> 00:55:18,939
(triumphant music)

1644
00:55:21,344 --> 00:55:22,198
- [Mike] Uh, one more push.

1645
00:55:22,198 --> 00:55:25,841
We can see the head
now, you're doing fine.

1646
00:55:25,841 --> 00:55:27,582
- [Servo] John Glenn sings
the great love songs.

1647
00:55:27,582 --> 00:55:29,876
- Attention all aircraft,
vicinity George Air Force Base.

1648
00:55:29,876 --> 00:55:31,237
Emergency has terminated.

1649
00:55:31,237 --> 00:55:33,482
George open for normal traffic.

1650
00:55:33,482 --> 00:55:36,031
- [Mike] That was a great scene.

1651
00:55:36,031 --> 00:55:40,198
- Hey Stinky, you leave
now, you're out of the band!

1652
00:55:42,348 --> 00:55:44,693
- [Mike] That guys got a poster
of Mark Spitz in his locker.

1653
00:55:44,693 --> 00:55:45,741
- Who doesn't?

1654
00:55:45,741 --> 00:55:46,990
- You were the one they're making

1655
00:55:46,990 --> 00:55:48,230
all of that fuss about out there.

1656
00:55:48,230 --> 00:55:50,085
Hey, uh, you trying to
grab a satellite, boy?

1657
00:55:50,085 --> 00:55:52,228
- Mm-mm, it was a little
harry, but no sweat.

1658
00:55:52,228 --> 00:55:54,111
- Well, with all those wagons out there,

1659
00:55:54,111 --> 00:55:56,278
somebody must have
worked up a little sweat.

1660
00:55:56,278 --> 00:55:57,628
- Well, sorry I disappointed them.

1661
00:55:57,628 --> 00:55:58,461
- [Servo] Virginia Slim?

1662
00:55:58,461 --> 00:56:00,905
- Somebody's been trying to
get a hold of you all day.

1663
00:56:00,905 --> 00:56:01,738
Long distance.

1664
00:56:01,738 --> 00:56:04,246
You're supposed to call, um, operator 12,

1665
00:56:04,246 --> 00:56:05,942
Washington, D.C.

1666
00:56:05,942 --> 00:56:06,875
- Right, thanks Gene.

1667
00:56:06,875 --> 00:56:09,333
- Hey, hey, do you have
any influence back there?

1668
00:56:09,333 --> 00:56:12,359
(mock laughter)

1669
00:56:12,359 --> 00:56:13,398
- Oh, nothing's wrong, Johnny.

1670
00:56:13,398 --> 00:56:14,898
We hadn't heard from you for a while,

1671
00:56:14,898 --> 00:56:16,546
and we were wondering if
everything's all right out there.

1672
00:56:16,546 --> 00:56:17,385
- [Servo] Yeah, is it?

1673
00:56:17,385 --> 00:56:18,900
- Oh Dad, everything's okay.

1674
00:56:18,900 --> 00:56:19,765
- [Mike] I just hate you.

1675
00:56:19,765 --> 00:56:21,618
- Hey, it's great to
hear from ya, how are ya?

1676
00:56:21,618 --> 00:56:23,193
- Feelin' tops, Johnny.

1677
00:56:23,193 --> 00:56:24,421
- [Mike] I miss Scott Thorson.

1678
00:56:24,421 --> 00:56:25,781
- But I was concerned about

1679
00:56:25,781 --> 00:56:27,370
not hearing from you for so long.

1680
00:56:27,370 --> 00:56:29,908
- Oh I'm sorry, Dad, we've
been so busy here lately,

1681
00:56:29,908 --> 00:56:32,249
I guess I've been kind of lax
in writing to you and Mom.

1682
00:56:32,249 --> 00:56:33,082
- [Servo] Well, bye.

1683
00:56:33,082 --> 00:56:33,915
- How is she?

1684
00:56:33,915 --> 00:56:36,980
- Fine as usual, but you know
how she worries about you.

1685
00:56:36,980 --> 00:56:38,218
- [Mike] This guy's Uncle Bead. (laughter)

1686
00:56:38,218 --> 00:56:40,297
- In all the time that
I was flying years ago,

1687
00:56:40,297 --> 00:56:42,389
I couldn't convince her how safe it was.

1688
00:56:42,389 --> 00:56:43,935
- And now you're worried
about me, huh Dad?

1689
00:56:43,935 --> 00:56:44,768
- [Servo] Okay bye.

1690
00:56:44,768 --> 00:56:46,828
- Tell me, how's it going,
Johnny, any troubles?

1691
00:56:46,828 --> 00:56:48,435
- Oh, nothing at all to speak of.

1692
00:56:48,435 --> 00:56:50,243
We're going through the
typical transition training

1693
00:56:50,243 --> 00:56:51,980
that everybody does in these 104s.

1694
00:56:51,980 --> 00:56:53,344
- Yes, I imagine you are.

1695
00:56:53,344 --> 00:56:54,761
- [Mike] Yes, I imagine so.

1696
00:56:54,761 --> 00:56:57,159
- Trouble is, is that, I've
been reading a number of reports

1697
00:56:57,159 --> 00:56:58,994
lately that come across my desk

1698
00:56:58,994 --> 00:57:01,280
telling me of all sorts of accidents.

1699
00:57:01,280 --> 00:57:02,776
- Accidents, what kind?

1700
00:57:02,776 --> 00:57:03,777
- Put dad on the line.

1701
00:57:03,777 --> 00:57:04,860
- Usual kind.

1702
00:57:05,835 --> 00:57:08,344
Engine flame out, things like that.

1703
00:57:08,344 --> 00:57:09,395
- [Servo] Drift of the page.

1704
00:57:09,395 --> 00:57:11,840
- In the fighters, the
pilot always bails out.

1705
00:57:11,840 --> 00:57:13,241
Not like in those big jobs where you

1706
00:57:13,241 --> 00:57:15,903
keep flying if you loose one engine.

1707
00:57:15,903 --> 00:57:17,898
- Oh, look Dad, I know
what you're driving at,

1708
00:57:17,898 --> 00:57:19,281
and the whole thing is silly.

1709
00:57:19,281 --> 00:57:21,169
There's been nothing
like that happening here,

1710
00:57:21,169 --> 00:57:23,565
and if it did, I'm sure I
could hack any emergency

1711
00:57:23,565 --> 00:57:26,214
where we go through these
recommended steps all the time.

1712
00:57:26,214 --> 00:57:28,805
- I still wish you'd apply for a transfer,

1713
00:57:28,805 --> 00:57:30,405
into a bigger outfit, you know.

1714
00:57:30,405 --> 00:57:33,742
- [Mike] Your father
and I are worried, son.

1715
00:57:33,742 --> 00:57:36,952
- Those B-58s will be coming
into their own shortly.

1716
00:57:36,952 --> 00:57:38,837
- But Dad, it just isn't done that way.

1717
00:57:38,837 --> 00:57:40,968
You don't go hopping
around from place to place

1718
00:57:40,968 --> 00:57:42,936
because you want to try
out different methods.

1719
00:57:42,936 --> 00:57:43,769
- [Mike] Dad.

1720
00:57:43,769 --> 00:57:44,958
- Well, you should know how they operate.

1721
00:57:44,958 --> 00:57:47,488
- I'm in a position to make
it real easy for you to get

1722
00:57:47,488 --> 00:57:51,099
into an operational B-52
wing right away, Johnny.

1723
00:57:51,099 --> 00:57:53,955
- I'm sorry, that doesn't
interest me in the least.

1724
00:57:53,955 --> 00:57:56,340
- For heaven's sake, boy, I'm interested.

1725
00:57:56,340 --> 00:57:57,519
- Come on, Dad.

1726
00:57:57,519 --> 00:57:59,650
Look, I'm here to stay, and no one

1727
00:57:59,650 --> 00:58:01,019
is going to change my mind.

1728
00:58:01,019 --> 00:58:04,160
- [Servo] I got life in me, big daddy.

1729
00:58:04,160 --> 00:58:06,275
- Why John, I'm sorry I intruded.

1730
00:58:06,275 --> 00:58:07,427
- [Mike] This guy's Maude Frickert.

1731
00:58:07,427 --> 00:58:09,246
- Merely thinking of your
future as any fathers

1732
00:58:09,246 --> 00:58:11,201
who's interested in his son's vocation.

1733
00:58:11,201 --> 00:58:13,297
- Dad, I sure appreciate your calling,

1734
00:58:13,297 --> 00:58:14,641
but I just got down from a flight,

1735
00:58:14,641 --> 00:58:16,655
and I've got to report
to a debriefing session.

1736
00:58:16,655 --> 00:58:17,500
You understand.

1737
00:58:17,500 --> 00:58:18,615
- My arms are killing me.

1738
00:58:18,615 --> 00:58:20,044
