- Go ahead, ops.

1987
01:07:05,221 --> 01:07:07,307
- We have a sever weather warning, sir.

1988
01:07:07,307 --> 01:07:09,850
That front turned
northeast, picked up speed

1989
01:07:09,850 --> 01:07:11,944
after it left Mexico.

1990
01:07:11,944 --> 01:07:13,492
They've reported thunderstorms,

1991
01:07:13,492 --> 01:07:16,081
high winds, extreme turbulence,

1992
01:07:16,081 --> 01:07:18,821
and maximum cloud tops to 45,000 feet.

1993
01:07:18,821 --> 01:07:19,654
- [Mike] There, you old.

1994
01:07:19,654 --> 01:07:20,585
- [Voiceover] Are we clear?

1995
01:07:20,585 --> 01:07:21,633
- [Mike] I don't know.

1996
01:07:21,633 --> 01:07:22,944
- The base is, sir,

1997
01:07:22,944 --> 01:07:24,480
but we have that flight of four birds

1998
01:07:24,480 --> 01:07:25,668
on a refueling mission.

1999
01:07:25,668 --> 01:07:26,895
- [Servo] Birds?

2000
01:07:26,895 --> 01:07:28,470
Look at the birdies.

2001
01:07:28,470 --> 01:07:29,807
- Front is moving so fast,

2002
01:07:29,807 --> 01:07:31,330
that it might cut them off from us

2003
01:07:31,330 --> 01:07:32,766
before they have a chance to realize it.

2004
01:07:32,766 --> 01:07:33,599
- [Voiceover] Who's out?

2005
01:07:33,599 --> 01:07:35,782
- Major Stevens, Lieutenants York,

2006
01:07:35,782 --> 01:07:37,493
Lyons, and Witkowski.

2007
01:07:37,493 --> 01:07:38,326
- [Mike] Stevens?

2008
01:07:38,326 --> 01:07:39,432
- All from the 578th.

2009
01:07:39,432 --> 01:07:40,487
- [Voiceover] They know what to do,

2010
01:07:40,487 --> 01:07:41,626
and they have sufficient fuel

2011
01:07:41,626 --> 01:07:43,395
to find an alternate
in case they get stuck.

2012
01:07:43,395 --> 01:07:44,977
Keep me informed as they come in.

2013
01:07:44,977 --> 01:07:47,961
- [Servo] This movie has
severe contraindications.

2014
01:07:47,961 --> 01:07:49,420
- [Voiceover] George
tower, this is Cordite one.

2015
01:07:49,420 --> 01:07:50,735
Request landing information, over.

2016
01:07:50,735 --> 01:07:51,706
- Cordite one, George tower,

2017
01:07:51,706 --> 01:07:55,052
land runway one six,
winds 170 at 20 knotts

2018
01:07:55,052 --> 01:07:57,202
gusting to 30, call on downwind with gear.

2019
01:07:57,202 --> 01:07:58,535
- Remember FDIC.

2020
01:08:00,377 --> 01:08:01,544
- [Servo] Hey.

2021
01:08:03,069 --> 01:08:04,278
- Wing ops to wing commander.

2022
01:08:04,278 --> 01:08:05,111
- Go ahead, ops.

2023
01:08:05,111 --> 01:08:07,396
- Major Stevens just
called in for a landing.

2024
01:08:07,396 --> 01:08:08,749
He's on the pattern now.

2025
01:08:08,749 --> 01:08:09,661
- [Voiceover] Stevens already?

2026
01:08:09,661 --> 01:08:10,648
He takes on fuel last.

2027
01:08:10,648 --> 01:08:11,958
He's supposed to be the last one in.

2028
01:08:11,958 --> 01:08:13,931
I'll be right out there.

2029
01:08:13,931 --> 01:08:15,348
- [Servo] Oh boy.

2030
01:08:16,696 --> 01:08:20,059
- [Mike] I had to go potty, I'm sorry.

2031
01:08:20,059 --> 01:08:21,443
- What are you doing in so early

2032
01:08:21,443 --> 01:08:22,645
without the rest of your troops?

2033
01:08:22,645 --> 01:08:23,824
- Well, it was getting
so sloppy out there,

2034
01:08:23,824 --> 01:08:25,293
I cut my cross country short.

2035
01:08:25,293 --> 01:08:26,346
- Apparently no one else did.

2036
01:08:26,346 --> 01:08:27,362
You're the only one back.

2037
01:08:27,362 --> 01:08:28,195
- [Servo] Shut up.

2038
01:08:28,195 --> 01:08:29,028
- I wasn't going to set
her down in some alternate

2039
01:08:29,028 --> 01:08:30,346
when I knew I could get in here easily.

2040
01:08:30,346 --> 01:08:31,859
- Sure, but why didn't your flight do it?

2041
01:08:31,859 --> 01:08:33,135
- Colonel, we both know they can put in to

2042
01:08:33,135 --> 01:08:34,779
Nellis, Marks, Luke.

2043
01:08:34,779 --> 01:08:36,105
- [Servo] Joshua, Judges.

2044
01:08:36,105 --> 01:08:38,110
- Half a dozen other places
I gave them during briefing.

2045
01:08:38,110 --> 01:08:39,569
That's exactly what
they're supposed to do.

2046
01:08:39,569 --> 01:08:40,664
I can find out what's going on

2047
01:08:40,664 --> 01:08:41,604
a lot easier from here

2048
01:08:41,604 --> 01:08:42,680
in case we get socked in.

2049
01:08:42,680 --> 01:08:44,095
- We won't, it'll stay clear here.

2050
01:08:44,095 --> 01:08:44,928
- [Mike] Ah.

2051
01:08:44,928 --> 01:08:46,845
- Let's talk refueling.

2052
01:08:47,802 --> 01:08:48,635
(ringing)

2053
01:08:48,635 --> 01:08:50,072
- [Servo] Even their phones are sunburnt.

2054
01:08:50,072 --> 01:08:51,479
- [Voiceover] Tower just received a report

2055
01:08:51,479 --> 01:08:53,361
from the San Bernardino
County sheriff's office.

2056
01:08:53,361 --> 01:08:54,260
- [Servo] Huh, huh?

2057
01:08:54,260 --> 01:08:55,093
- [Voiceover] A local rancher observed

2058
01:08:55,093 --> 01:08:56,263
a jet fighter go down.

2059
01:08:56,263 --> 01:08:57,142
- [Servo] Who is this?

2060
01:08:57,142 --> 01:08:58,664
What do you want, leave me alone!

2061
01:08:58,664 --> 01:09:00,548
- [Voiceover] Location
was the Granite Mountains.

2062
01:09:00,548 --> 01:09:02,450
and east of Apple Valley.

2063
01:09:02,450 --> 01:09:03,438
- [Mike] Aw.

2064
01:09:03,438 --> 01:09:05,438
- Steve-o to the rescue!

2065
01:09:06,328 --> 01:09:09,184
- [Mike] It's Budgie, the helicopter.

2066
01:09:09,184 --> 01:09:10,727
- [Servo] And they're off to the rescue

2067
01:09:10,727 --> 01:09:12,630
in a highly dangerous prototype.

2068
01:09:12,630 --> 01:09:13,964
- How do it work?

2069
01:09:13,964 --> 01:09:15,231
- [Servo] They go round and round.

2070
01:09:15,231 --> 01:09:17,861
- (goofy laughter) Cool.

2071
01:09:17,861 --> 01:09:19,579
- [Mike] Ooh, the suites.

2072
01:09:19,579 --> 01:09:23,213
- Uh, we're going to go
higher than this, aren't we?

2073
01:09:23,213 --> 01:09:26,213
(mimics propellers)

2074
01:09:28,915 --> 01:09:31,118
- Oh, Shirley Muldowney just went by.

2075
01:09:31,118 --> 01:09:32,569
- I'm going to get the weather.

2076
01:09:32,569 --> 01:09:34,021
- [Mike] Hi, it's me.

2077
01:09:34,021 --> 01:09:35,392
- Tower, this is Major Stevens

2078
01:09:35,392 --> 01:09:36,627
in the wing commander's office.

2079
01:09:36,627 --> 01:09:38,188
What buzzed us just now?

2080
01:09:38,188 --> 01:09:40,536
- That was a 104 with
his gear down, major.

2081
01:09:40,536 --> 01:09:41,862
We didn't get any call from him,

2082
01:09:41,862 --> 01:09:44,041
so I assume he has an electrical failure.

2083
01:09:44,041 --> 01:09:46,005
He's turning on his final approach now.

2084
01:09:46,005 --> 01:09:48,929
(muffled talk)

2085
01:09:48,929 --> 01:09:50,431
- [Servo] Oh, once again the film

2086
01:09:50,431 --> 01:09:52,764
takes us in a new direction.

2087
01:09:53,860 --> 01:09:56,096
- What's the aircraft's number?

2088
01:09:56,096 --> 01:09:58,163
- It's a tough to tick him out, sir.

2089
01:09:58,163 --> 01:10:00,526
- [Voiceover] Standby one, sir.

2090
01:10:00,526 --> 01:10:01,941
- [Servo] Oh, is that real?

2091
01:10:01,941 --> 01:10:04,202
- [Mike] I'm bettin' ya.

2092
01:10:04,202 --> 01:10:06,931
- Sir, that was niner two
six that just touched.

2093
01:10:06,931 --> 01:10:07,764
- Okay.

2094
01:10:07,764 --> 01:10:10,268
- [Mike] Lunch today,
tomato soup, tater tots.

2095
01:10:10,268 --> 01:10:12,106
- Squadron ops in wing commander's office.

2096
01:10:12,106 --> 01:10:13,334
Who was up in 926?

2097
01:10:13,334 --> 01:10:14,167
- Hmm?

2098
01:10:14,167 --> 01:10:15,281
Do we have to leave now?

2099
01:10:15,281 --> 01:10:16,123
- [Mike] Yeah.

2100
01:10:16,123 --> 01:10:16,956
- [Crow] Getting into it.

2101
01:10:16,956 --> 01:10:18,037
- [Mike] Miss it.

2102
01:10:18,037 --> 01:10:18,870
- Sir?

2103
01:10:18,870 --> 01:10:20,094
- Come on!

2104
01:10:20,094 --> 01:10:22,751
- 926 was taken up by Lieutenant York.

2105
01:10:22,751 --> 01:10:26,001
(slamming and beeping)

2106
01:10:34,768 --> 01:10:35,659
- Welcome, my friends.

2107
01:10:35,659 --> 01:10:37,186
We are very fortunate
to have with us today

2108
01:10:37,186 --> 01:10:39,379
the The United Servo Academy Men's Chorus,

2109
01:10:39,379 --> 01:10:42,699
directed by United Servo
Academy Men's choral director,

2110
01:10:42,699 --> 01:10:45,198
Vice Brigadiere Sir Thomas Bowlhead Servo,

2111
01:10:45,198 --> 01:10:48,230
conducting them in the United
Servo Academy Men's Chorus,

2112
01:10:48,230 --> 01:10:49,063
uh, hymn.

2113
01:10:50,345 --> 01:10:52,333
- [Servo] All right, eyes front.

2114
01:10:52,333 --> 01:10:53,250
Three, and.

2115
01:10:54,600 --> 01:10:58,367
♫ Here's to the guys and

2116
01:10:58,367 --> 01:11:01,617
♫ Gals who like to fly

2117
01:11:02,643 --> 01:11:06,291
♫ Flying so high with some

2118
01:11:06,291 --> 01:11:09,041
♫ Guy in the sky

2119
01:11:10,694 --> 01:11:14,145
♫ Sky rockets in flight

2120
01:11:14,145 --> 01:11:18,145
♫ Afternoon delight happen high

2121
01:11:19,333 --> 01:11:22,166
♫ At your service

2122
01:11:26,849 --> 01:11:29,527
♫ Would you like to fly

2123
01:11:29,527 --> 01:11:33,027
♫ In my beautiful balloon

2124
01:11:34,803 --> 01:11:37,285
♫ Take these broken wings

2125
01:11:37,285 --> 01:11:41,452
♫ And learn to fly me to the moon

2126
01:11:42,583 --> 01:11:46,721
♫ Sail on a silver bird

2127
01:11:46,721 --> 01:11:50,888
♫ Have you ever heard
that the bird is the word

2128
01:11:53,881 --> 01:11:57,252
♫ In a big country

2129
01:11:57,252 --> 01:12:00,502
♫ Dreams stay with you

2130
01:12:01,387 --> 01:12:05,280
♫ Come along with me, Lucille,

2131
01:12:05,280 --> 01:12:09,504
♫ In my merry Oldsmobile

2132
01:12:09,504 --> 01:12:13,245
♫ We are kids for saving earth

2133
01:12:13,245 --> 01:12:17,588
♫ We are fans of Colin Firth

2134
01:12:17,588 --> 01:12:21,086
♫ Off we go to yonder blue

2135
01:12:21,086 --> 01:12:25,253
♫ We really move our tails for you

2136
01:12:28,877 --> 01:12:33,044
♫ 'Cross the wide Missouri ♫

2137
01:12:42,324 --> 01:12:43,601
- Ah.

2138
01:12:43,601 --> 01:12:45,932
Ah, fantastic, absolutely fantastic.

2139
01:12:45,932 --> 01:12:48,566
That was the United Servo
Academy Men's Chorus,

2140
01:12:48,566 --> 01:12:51,137
and that sonorous tone
that you heard, of course,

2141
01:12:51,137 --> 01:12:53,018
has to be due in large part to the

2142
01:12:53,018 --> 01:12:55,754
fantastic conducting, what are
you doing? (chorus singing)

2143
01:12:55,754 --> 01:12:56,672
What are you doing?

2144
01:12:56,672 --> 01:12:58,018
Please, stop that music, please.

2145
01:12:58,018 --> 01:12:59,618
Please do not, do not continue this,

2146
01:12:59,618 --> 01:13:01,214
Vice Brigadiere Sir Thomas Bowlhead.

2147
01:13:01,214 --> 01:13:02,898
I employ you stop the music!

2148
01:13:02,898 --> 01:13:05,079
Stop, I say, stop the music!

2149
01:13:05,079 --> 01:13:07,404
Uh, Sylvester, can we get
an engineer in here, please,

2150
01:13:07,404 --> 01:13:09,636
in studio A, I apologize,
ladies and gentlemen.

2151
01:13:09,636 --> 01:13:10,691
I want you out of my studio.

2152
01:13:10,691 --> 01:13:11,851
Stop this music right now.

2153
01:13:11,851 --> 01:13:13,342
Out, out!

2154
01:13:13,342 --> 01:13:14,259
Rows, rows!

2155
01:13:15,577 --> 01:13:17,224
- [Servo] (singing)
Rinky dinky parlez-vous.

2156
01:13:17,224 --> 01:13:19,468
- Weather says it's
stirring up east of us.

2157
01:13:19,468 --> 01:13:21,255
Storm was fast and
vicious but not too thick.

2158
01:13:21,255 --> 01:13:24,258
- Those choppers should get in there then.

2159
01:13:24,258 --> 01:13:26,401
(propellers)

2160
01:13:26,401 --> 01:13:28,008
- It's a smooth, smooth ride

2161
01:13:28,008 --> 01:13:30,531
thanks to the counter-rotating props.

2162
01:13:30,531 --> 01:13:31,932
(laughter)

2163
01:13:31,932 --> 01:13:34,015
Something's following us.

2164
01:13:36,812 --> 01:13:38,827
- [Servo] Ee-gah.

2165
01:13:38,827 --> 01:13:41,244
- [Crow] Look out for snakes.

2166
01:13:42,309 --> 01:13:43,280
- [Servo] Are they on a man hunt

2167
01:13:43,280 --> 01:13:46,076
for Juan Del Dez or somethin'?

2168
01:13:46,076 --> 01:13:47,504
- It's still following us.

2169
01:13:47,504 --> 01:13:49,772
- Now, keep us informed
if they call in at all,

2170
01:13:49,772 --> 01:13:51,216
and how about checking with
some of those alternates

2171
01:13:51,216 --> 01:13:52,681
to see if they radioed in there.

2172
01:13:52,681 --> 01:13:53,514
- [Mike] Okay.

2173
01:13:53,514 --> 01:13:55,076
- And tell Lieutenant
York I want to see him

2174
01:13:55,076 --> 01:13:56,446
in Colonel Hunt's office immediately.

2175
01:13:56,446 --> 01:13:58,001
- [Mike] He has a cab forward skull.

2176
01:13:58,001 --> 01:13:59,546
- Still no word from rescue.

2177
01:13:59,546 --> 01:14:02,435
(ringing)

2178
01:14:02,435 --> 01:14:03,710
Colonel Hunt's office.

2179
01:14:03,710 --> 01:14:06,168
- Yes, well, I'd love to
see you again too, well, uh.

2180
01:14:06,168 --> 01:14:07,941
- Well, (stammers) yes, just a moment.

2181
01:14:07,941 --> 01:14:09,704
- It's Mom, and she's mad.

2182
01:14:09,704 --> 01:14:11,671
- Here's one for the books.

2183
01:14:11,671 --> 01:14:14,115
Congressman Witkowski is on the line.

2184
01:14:14,115 --> 01:14:14,948
- What!

2185
01:14:14,948 --> 01:14:16,080
How could he know?

2186
01:14:16,080 --> 01:14:17,092
(gulp)

2187
01:14:17,092 --> 01:14:18,791
Tell him I'm in a conference
with the general or,

2188
01:14:18,791 --> 01:14:20,193
ah, I better take it.

2189
01:14:20,193 --> 01:14:21,764
It's a hell of a way to run a railroad.

2190
01:14:21,764 --> 01:14:23,158
- [Mike] God, my face is big.

2191
01:14:23,158 --> 01:14:24,200
- Colonel Hunt here.

2192
01:14:24,200 --> 01:14:25,286
- Hello, Colonel Hunt.

2193
01:14:25,286 --> 01:14:26,119
- [Servo] Ah.

2194
01:14:26,119 --> 01:14:27,451
- This is John Witkowski.

2195
01:14:27,451 --> 01:14:29,288
We haven't talked together
for a few months now,

2196
01:14:29,288 --> 01:14:32,092
so I was calling to get
some information from you.

2197
01:14:32,092 --> 01:14:33,220
- What's your hat size?

2198
01:14:33,220 --> 01:14:34,834
- It's nice to hear from you again, but I.

2199
01:14:34,834 --> 01:14:37,002
- Sorry I seem like a pest, Colonel, but.

2200
01:14:37,002 --> 01:14:37,835
- [Mike] Yeah.

2201
01:14:37,835 --> 01:14:39,109
- You remember how when we were in,

2202
01:14:39,109 --> 01:14:41,115
we didn't always write home
as much as we should have.

2203
01:14:41,115 --> 01:14:43,214
- [Mike] Look, you ran a bakery.

2204
01:14:43,214 --> 01:14:44,659
- My boy, John, is guilty of

2205
01:14:44,659 --> 01:14:46,261
doing the same thing, so I thought.

2206
01:14:46,261 --> 01:14:47,504
- Congressman, I'm still in there service,

2207
01:14:47,504 --> 01:14:49,703
and I agree, I don't write
home too much anymore either.

2208
01:14:49,703 --> 01:14:51,804
- Well, I was only wondering
how the boy was doing

2209
01:14:51,804 --> 01:14:53,959
there in training and all that.

2210
01:14:53,959 --> 01:14:55,969
- Sir, as far as I know,
you're boy is doing

2211
01:14:55,969 --> 01:14:57,689
as well as could be expected,

2212
01:14:57,689 --> 01:14:59,413
but right now, I must
be brief and hang up.

2213
01:14:59,413 --> 01:15:01,637
We're having an important
exercise here at the base,

2214
01:15:01,637 --> 01:15:03,538
and I need the lines for
communication purposes.

2215
01:15:03,538 --> 01:15:07,381
- [Voiceover] Wing ops.
- [Servo] Groin patrol.

2216
01:15:07,381 --> 01:15:08,423
- Go ahead, ops.

2217
01:15:08,423 --> 01:15:10,596
- The helicopter pilots find the plane.

2218
01:15:10,596 --> 01:15:12,021
It's a 104, sir.

2219
01:15:12,021 --> 01:15:12,854
- [Servo] Ah.

2220
01:15:12,854 --> 01:15:14,341
- They came across it
in a pretty rugged area.

2221
01:15:14,341 --> 01:15:15,174
- Ooh, yeah.

2222
01:15:15,174 --> 01:15:16,647
- They found the pilot had ejected.

2223
01:15:16,647 --> 01:15:17,852
They're looking for the chute now.

2224
01:15:17,852 --> 01:15:19,452
- What was the number of the down plane?

2225
01:15:19,452 --> 01:15:20,701
- [Mike] Uh, four.

2226
01:15:20,701 --> 01:15:23,589
- [Voiceover] I don't know,
sir, they didn't give it to us.

2227
01:15:23,589 --> 01:15:25,747
- Well, contact them,
get the number, quick.

2228
01:15:25,747 --> 01:15:27,167
- [Hunt] Sorry to be blunt, congressman,

2229
01:15:27,167 --> 01:15:28,506
but I have to cut this conversation short

2230
01:15:28,506 --> 01:15:30,126
so to keep all of our lines clear.

2231
01:15:30,126 --> 01:15:32,549
I'll see to it that your son calls you.

2232
01:15:32,549 --> 01:15:34,675
- [Mike] My, that was blunt.

2233
01:15:34,675 --> 01:15:36,432
- (knocking) [Stevens] Come in!

2234
01:15:36,432 --> 01:15:37,509
- [Servo] Found him, he was under

2235
01:15:37,509 --> 01:15:38,831
a pile of blankets in my room.

2236
01:15:38,831 --> 01:15:40,014
- So what happened to you?

2237
01:15:40,014 --> 01:15:41,208
- Both of my generators went out, sir,

2238
01:15:41,208 --> 01:15:42,713
and I couldn't get them back on the line.

2239
01:15:42,713 --> 01:15:43,973
- I mean with that front moving in on you,

2240
01:15:43,973 --> 01:15:44,923
what did you do?

2241
01:15:44,923 --> 01:15:46,895
- Well, actually it wasn't
too bad where I was, sir.

2242
01:15:46,895 --> 01:15:48,055
I flew around easterly end of it,

2243
01:15:48,055 --> 01:15:48,935
(poking sound effect)

2244
01:15:48,935 --> 01:15:49,974
and came up from behind.

2245
01:15:49,974 --> 01:15:51,170
- Do you realize Lyons and Witkowski

2246
01:15:51,170 --> 01:15:52,071
haven't checked in yet?

2247
01:15:52,071 --> 01:15:52,904
- Yes sir.

2248
01:15:52,904 --> 01:15:54,000
- [Mike] And I don't care.

2249
01:15:54,000 --> 01:15:55,204
- Although I did hear someone on the radio

2250
01:15:55,204 --> 01:15:56,837
say that they were going
to try to land at Nellis

2251
01:15:56,837 --> 01:15:58,437
instead of making it back here.

2252
01:15:58,437 --> 01:16:00,545
I didn't recognize the
voice or call sign though.

2253
01:16:00,545 --> 01:16:02,148
- [Voiceover] Wing ops to wing commander.

2254
01:16:02,148 --> 01:16:03,518
- [Hunt] Yeah, ops, any news for us?

2255
01:16:03,518 --> 01:16:05,837
- Rescue says that was 929 that crashed.

2256
01:16:05,837 --> 01:16:06,956
- [Hunt] Okay.

2257
01:16:06,956 --> 01:16:08,074
(ringing)

2258
01:16:08,074 --> 01:16:10,175
- [Servo] (laughs)
Rampant phone call action.

2259
01:16:10,175 --> 01:16:11,984
- Major, uh, flight
services just now called

2260
01:16:11,984 --> 01:16:13,561
to say that one of our
birds landed up in Nellis

2261
01:16:13,561 --> 01:16:14,874
a half an hour ago.

2262
01:16:14,874 --> 01:16:16,921
Said out by approaching front.

2263
01:16:16,921 --> 01:16:18,210
- [Servo] His chin must hurt.

2264
01:16:18,210 --> 01:16:19,503
- Yes sir, they got it so bad up there,

2265
01:16:19,503 --> 01:16:21,147
right now, he's staying on the ground.

2266
01:16:21,147 --> 01:16:22,575
Pilot's John Witkowski.

2267
01:16:22,575 --> 01:16:24,082
- Witkowski's safe at Nellis?

2268
01:16:24,082 --> 01:16:25,458
O'Brien, look at the scheduling port.

2269
01:16:25,458 --> 01:16:26,522
Did Lyons take up 929?

2270
01:16:26,522 --> 01:16:27,773
- 929?

2271
01:16:27,773 --> 01:16:28,973
- Ooh, Steve got doughnuts.

2272
01:16:28,973 --> 01:16:31,547
- Yes sir, that's assigned to Lyons.

2273
01:16:31,547 --> 01:16:32,743
- [Servo] She's rather obliging.

2274
01:16:32,743 --> 01:16:35,151
- Lieutenant Lyons is out there.

2275
01:16:35,151 --> 01:16:38,318
- [Mike] Roar, I'm king of the desert.

2276
01:16:39,391 --> 01:16:41,558
(humming)

2277
01:16:46,558 --> 01:16:49,432
- [Servo] Listen, he
must be the chosen one.

2278
01:16:49,432 --> 01:16:52,012
- It's called a North Star system.

2279
01:16:52,012 --> 01:16:54,179
(humming)

2280
01:16:55,391 --> 01:16:57,440
- [Mike] Capricorn one.

2281
01:16:57,440 --> 01:16:59,607
(humming)

2282
01:17:02,407 --> 01:17:05,929
- I'll signal them with my deodorant.

2283
01:17:05,929 --> 01:17:10,029
- [Mike] This stuff really
attracts helicopters.

2284
01:17:10,029 --> 01:17:12,844
(humming)

2285
01:17:12,844 --> 01:17:13,927
- [Servo] Oh.

2286
01:17:15,571 --> 01:17:17,988
Ah, hey look, it's a Fridays.

2287
01:17:19,651 --> 01:17:21,409
- Are the other armed services

2288
01:17:21,409 --> 01:17:24,774
as easy listening as the Air Force?

2289
01:17:24,774 --> 01:17:27,840
- [Mike] We have a visual ID on numbnuts.

2290
01:17:27,840 --> 01:17:29,430
(upbeat jazz)

2291
01:17:29,430 --> 01:17:32,930
- [Servo] Ah, it's a lush cocktail rescue.

2292
01:17:34,076 --> 01:17:36,243
(humming)

2293
01:17:40,852 --> 01:17:42,989
- [Mike] Ah yes.

2294
01:17:42,989 --> 01:17:44,116
Oh, it was pretty rough, man.

2295
01:17:44,116 --> 01:17:46,306
I had to eat a lizard and drink my urine.

2296
01:17:46,306 --> 01:17:47,598
- [Servo] But you were
only here for 10 minutes.

2297
01:17:47,598 --> 01:17:48,974
- [Mike] I know, but.

2298
01:17:48,974 --> 01:17:50,168
- Congratulations, you're the

2299
01:17:50,168 --> 01:17:52,947
recipient of today's lucky rescue.

2300
01:17:52,947 --> 01:17:55,804
- [Mike] I did things I'm not proud of.

2301
01:17:55,804 --> 01:18:00,525
- [Servo] (singing)
The day you rescued me.

2302
01:18:00,525 --> 01:18:03,277
Now, back to the club
for a smooth Canadian.

2303
01:18:03,277 --> 01:18:04,643
- [Mike] Is that how that goes?

2304
01:18:04,643 --> 01:18:05,643
- Found one.

2305
01:18:08,800 --> 01:18:10,681
(stammering)

2306
01:18:10,681 --> 01:18:11,984
- [Servo] Oh, it's that
counter-rotating plane!

2307
01:18:11,984 --> 01:18:14,401
I don't want to ride in this!

2308
01:18:15,905 --> 01:18:18,322
- At ease, Lieutenant Looser.

2309
01:18:20,862 --> 01:18:23,029
(humming)

2310
01:18:24,287 --> 01:18:27,864
- [Mike] Later, in large group econ.

2311
01:18:27,864 --> 01:18:29,655
- All right, you 104 drivers, settle down,

2312
01:18:29,655 --> 01:18:30,830
and listen to something important.

2313
01:18:30,830 --> 01:18:32,340
- [Servo] Jerry Van Dyke
has something to say.

2314
01:18:32,340 --> 01:18:33,677
- Thank you, major.

2315
01:18:33,677 --> 01:18:36,620
Well, that was some to do we
had around here yesterday,

2316
01:18:36,620 --> 01:18:37,824
so I'll get right to the point.

2317
01:18:37,824 --> 01:18:38,824
- I'm Scatman Crothers.

2318
01:18:38,824 --> 01:18:40,548
- Two of you did the right thing,

2319
01:18:40,548 --> 01:18:42,043
and one of you goofed up royally.

2320
01:18:42,043 --> 01:18:42,876
- [Servo] Jacques.

2321
01:18:42,876 --> 01:18:45,303
- So, we lost one badly needed aircraft.

2322
01:18:45,303 --> 01:18:46,866
Now, when you're in that high fast seat,

2323
01:18:46,866 --> 01:18:48,500
when you get your head up
where it doesn't belong,

2324
01:18:48,500 --> 01:18:49,870
you're going to find out
you're going to end up

2325
01:18:49,870 --> 01:18:51,374
with a short end of the stick.

2326
01:18:51,374 --> 01:18:53,355
- [Mike] Dickweed,
stand up and take a bow.

2327
01:18:53,355 --> 01:18:55,303
- Investigation board
will submit its findings

2328
01:18:55,303 --> 01:18:57,424
in a day so, so we'll
let it drop until then.

2329
01:18:57,424 --> 01:18:58,993
- [Servo] Then we'll kill ya.

2330
01:18:58,993 --> 01:19:00,593
- But I have some information

2331
01:19:00,593 --> 01:19:01,856
you've been waiting to hear.

2332
01:19:01,856 --> 01:19:03,709
- Marilu Henner is replacing Vicky.

2333
01:19:03,709 --> 01:19:06,966
- And your entire fire squadron, the 578,

2334
01:19:06,966 --> 01:19:10,087
deploy for Europe. (cheering)

2335
01:19:10,087 --> 01:19:10,920
- [Mike] Nice.

2336
01:19:10,920 --> 01:19:12,152
- [Servo] Class, class!

2337
01:19:12,152 --> 01:19:12,985
Shut up!

2338
01:19:14,105 --> 01:19:16,169
- Okay, okay, knock it off.

2339
01:19:16,169 --> 01:19:17,150
- [Servo] Thank you.

2340
01:19:17,150 --> 01:19:18,318
- You don't have to act as though

2341
01:19:18,318 --> 01:19:19,454
you didn't know it was coming.

2342
01:19:19,454 --> 01:19:20,562
- [Mike] Aw, eat it raw.

2343
01:19:20,562 --> 01:19:24,029
- 'Course we have a lot of
polishing up to do for the ORI,

2344
01:19:24,029 --> 01:19:26,875
and a lot of good old fashioned
paperwork to complete.

2345
01:19:26,875 --> 01:19:28,584
- [Mike] You're not funny.

2346
01:19:28,584 --> 01:19:30,174
- Since we'll be flying
our own Starfighters

2347
01:19:30,174 --> 01:19:31,777
over the wire,

2348
01:19:31,777 --> 01:19:34,356
you're going to have to check
out your rescue equipment.

2349
01:19:34,356 --> 01:19:35,494
- Check out this.

2350
01:19:35,494 --> 01:19:37,915
- Now, a very important piece
of that rescue equipment

2351
01:19:37,915 --> 01:19:40,199
is what we call a.

2352
01:19:40,199 --> 01:19:41,834
Sargent, would you step
up here for a moment?

2353
01:19:41,834 --> 01:19:43,626
- [Servo] The name's
Randy in the latest gear.

2354
01:19:43,626 --> 01:19:44,925
- [Stevens] Sargent here
is dressed in what is known

2355
01:19:44,925 --> 01:19:45,978
as a poopie suit.

2356
01:19:45,978 --> 01:19:46,913
- [All] Poopie suit?

2357
01:19:46,913 --> 01:19:48,584
- [Voiceover] Now, don't ask
me why they call it that,

2358
01:19:48,584 --> 01:19:50,422
but you'll be wearing one
of these on your way across.

2359
01:19:50,422 --> 01:19:51,255
- [Mike] Ew.

2360
01:19:51,255 --> 01:19:52,841
- [Stevens] So next Saturday,
you're going to get a chance

2361
01:19:52,841 --> 01:19:54,199
to check them and make
sure there aren't any.

2362
01:19:54,199 --> 01:19:55,333
- [Mike] Woo-hoo!

2363
01:19:55,333 --> 01:19:58,482
(catcalling)

2364
01:19:58,482 --> 01:19:59,994
(humming)

2365
01:19:59,994 --> 01:20:01,689
- Okay, you jocks, let's find out

2366
01:20:01,689 --> 01:20:02,856
why you didn't join the navy.

2367
01:20:02,856 --> 01:20:04,010
Last one in's a Gooney bird.

2368
01:20:04,010 --> 01:20:05,631
(mock laughing)

2369
01:20:05,631 --> 01:20:09,737
- [Mike] Oh why do they
get the ducky, sir?

2370
01:20:09,737 --> 01:20:12,257
(humming)

2371
01:20:12,257 --> 01:20:13,343
- [All] (sing) Poopie suit.

2372
01:20:13,343 --> 01:20:14,938
(humming)

2373
01:20:14,938 --> 01:20:16,299
- [All] (sing) Poopie suit.

2374
01:20:16,299 --> 01:20:17,455
(humming)

2375
01:20:17,455 --> 01:20:18,582
- All right, men, poop!

2376
01:20:18,582 --> 01:20:19,772
- [Servo And Mike] (sing) Poopie suit.

2377
01:20:19,772 --> 01:20:21,221
(humming)

2378
01:20:21,221 --> 01:20:22,379
- [servo And Mike] (sing) Poopie suit.

2379
01:20:22,379 --> 01:20:24,432
(silly noises)

2380
01:20:24,432 --> 01:20:25,347
- [Servo And Mike] (sing) Poopie suit.

2381
01:20:25,347 --> 01:20:26,968
(silly noises)

2382
01:20:26,968 --> 01:20:28,266
- [Servo] (singing) You
poop it in your pants,

2383
01:20:28,266 --> 01:20:30,089
and you do a crazy pants,
it's a two piece suit.

2384
01:20:30,089 --> 01:20:32,613
- [Mike] (sings) Poopie suit.

2385
01:20:32,613 --> 01:20:35,196
(upbeat music)

2386
01:20:39,003 --> 01:20:40,804
- Colonel Hunt, telephone, sir.

2387
01:20:40,804 --> 01:20:42,138
- You mean they traced me here?

2388
01:20:42,138 --> 01:20:43,905
- You can take it on the inside extension.

2389
01:20:43,905 --> 01:20:44,980
- Okay, what is it?

2390
01:20:44,980 --> 01:20:46,846
- Aw, it's poopie suit day.

2391
01:20:46,846 --> 01:20:48,738
- You're a hard man to
locate, Colonel Hunt.

2392
01:20:48,738 --> 01:20:49,719
- [Mike] Oh geez.

2393
01:20:49,719 --> 01:20:50,974
- This is John Witkowski.

2394
01:20:50,974 --> 01:20:54,560
- Oh, right, sir, and how
are you again, congressman?

2395
01:20:54,560 --> 01:20:55,622
- I'm fine here.

2396
01:20:55,622 --> 01:20:57,276
- [Mike] Over there, not so good.

2397
01:20:57,276 --> 01:20:59,882
- Just now received information
through my committee

2398
01:20:59,882 --> 01:21:01,205
that you had an unfortunate loss

2399
01:21:01,205 --> 01:21:02,929
for another plane out there,

2400
01:21:02,929 --> 01:21:06,008
that my son was involved
in the same flight.

2401
01:21:06,008 --> 01:21:08,741
- Mr. Witkowski, we did
not loose another plane.

2402
01:21:08,741 --> 01:21:09,815
- [Servo] We misplaced it.

2403
01:21:09,815 --> 01:21:11,367
- That was the only one this past year.

2404
01:21:11,367 --> 01:21:13,923
- [Mike] Oh wait, except for those six.

2405
01:21:13,923 --> 01:21:15,247
- The wisest one on the flight

2406
01:21:15,247 --> 01:21:17,462
since he chose to land rather
than fight his way through.

2407
01:21:17,462 --> 01:21:19,476
- Just the same, Colonel,
when we were flying together,

2408
01:21:19,476 --> 01:21:20,855
you know as well as I do

2409
01:21:20,855 --> 01:21:23,665
that drastic action was
taken on such occasion.

2410
01:21:23,665 --> 01:21:26,186
- But we didn't have the poopie suit!

2411
01:21:26,186 --> 01:21:28,722
- Recall that we ever did fly together.

2412
01:21:28,722 --> 01:21:30,697
Furthermore, the proper
and prescribed action

2413
01:21:30,697 --> 01:21:32,243
was taken in the case immediately.

2414
01:21:32,243 --> 01:21:34,040
- Colonel Hunt, will you please inform me

2415
01:21:34,040 --> 01:21:36,421
as to why you are so stubborn

2416
01:21:36,421 --> 01:21:39,731
and will not consider
a transfer for my son?

2417
01:21:39,731 --> 01:21:42,442
- Why congressman, I wanted
to tell you about that.

2418
01:21:42,442 --> 01:21:43,934
As a matter of fact, we are

2419
01:21:43,934 --> 01:21:46,533
effecting a transfer for your boy.

2420
01:21:46,533 --> 01:21:48,121
- You what?

2421
01:21:48,121 --> 01:21:49,856
Wonderful, wonderful.

2422
01:21:49,856 --> 01:21:52,637
- [Mike] (singing) It's
wonderful, wonderful.

2423
01:21:52,637 --> 01:21:54,209
- When did all this happen?

2424
01:21:54,209 --> 01:21:56,004
- Only a couple weeks ago.

2425
01:21:56,004 --> 01:21:58,236
As a matter of fact, they're giving them a

2426
01:21:58,236 --> 01:22:00,328
sort of going away party right now.

2427
01:22:00,328 --> 01:22:01,664
- [Mike] His face is being eaten away.

2428
01:22:01,664 --> 01:22:03,121
- I'm sure he can give you
the good news by himself

2429
01:22:03,121 --> 01:22:04,353
since you're on the line.

2430
01:22:04,353 --> 01:22:05,949
You hold on, I'll get him for you.

2431
01:22:05,949 --> 01:22:06,949
- Yes, sure.

2432
01:22:08,938 --> 01:22:10,337
- I was in a holding ring.

2433
01:22:10,337 --> 01:22:13,281
They kept pushing me under. (mock sobbing)

2434
01:22:13,281 --> 01:22:16,296
(mimics electricity buzz)

2435
01:22:16,296 --> 01:22:17,906
- Hi Dad.

2436
01:22:17,906 --> 01:22:19,573
- Johnny, how goes it?

2437
01:22:19,573 --> 01:22:20,785
- Just great, Dad.

2438
01:22:20,785 --> 01:22:21,659
- Bye!

2439
01:22:21,659 --> 01:22:23,068
- Did the CO tell you the news?

2440
01:22:23,068 --> 01:22:25,235
- Yes, yes, he told me
you're being transferred,

2441
01:22:25,235 --> 01:22:26,830
but he didn't brief me in
on it, I think it's great.

2442
01:22:26,830 --> 01:22:28,133
- [Mike] Yes, yes.

2443
01:22:28,133 --> 01:22:29,976
- Which big outfit are you getting into?

2444
01:22:29,976 --> 01:22:31,013
- No, none, Dad.

2445
01:22:31,013 --> 01:22:33,303
Our entire squadron is
being transferred to Europe

2446
01:22:33,303 --> 01:22:35,273
to replace the squadron that's returning.

2447
01:22:35,273 --> 01:22:36,106
- [Mike] Doh.

2448
01:22:36,106 --> 01:22:37,284
- But I'll give you
and Mom all the details

2449
01:22:37,284 --> 01:22:38,778
in the letter, okay?

2450
01:22:38,778 --> 01:22:39,945
I promise you.

2451
01:22:41,556 --> 01:22:42,389
Dad.

2452
01:22:43,239 --> 01:22:44,906
- He's vapor locked.

2453
01:22:45,863 --> 01:22:47,299
- Hey Dad.

2454
01:22:47,299 --> 01:22:48,132
- [Servo] Dad, I just really need

2455
01:22:48,132 --> 01:22:49,177
your love and support right

2456
01:22:49,177 --> 01:22:51,117
now, and (mimics click)
Dad. (mimics click)

2457
01:22:51,117 --> 01:22:52,274
- [Mike] Well, I.

2458
01:22:52,274 --> 01:22:54,112
- And you mean he didn't say anything,

2459
01:22:54,112 --> 01:22:55,797
wasn't even angry or something?

2460
01:22:55,797 --> 01:22:57,100
- [Servo] Is he picking mints?

2461
01:22:57,100 --> 01:22:59,184
- Nothing he could do about it.

2462
01:22:59,184 --> 01:23:02,183
Oh, down deep inside, Dad knows
I made the right decision.

2463
01:23:02,183 --> 01:23:04,163
- I think you have too, Johnny.

2464
01:23:04,163 --> 01:23:05,833
Flying fighters is important to you,

2465
01:23:05,833 --> 01:23:08,407
and you wouldn't be happy
doing anything else,

2466
01:23:08,407 --> 01:23:11,202
but I sure hate to see you go.

2467
01:23:11,202 --> 01:23:12,447
- Will you miss me?

2468
01:23:12,447 --> 01:23:13,280
- Right.

2469
01:23:14,728 --> 01:23:16,349
- How often will you write?

2470
01:23:16,349 --> 01:23:18,105
- Is every day often enough?

2471
01:23:18,105 --> 01:23:20,802
- Well, just about, no less.

2472
01:23:20,802 --> 01:23:21,854
- [Servo] Wanna play refueling?

2473
01:23:21,854 --> 01:23:23,619
- How long will you be gone, Johnny?

2474
01:23:23,619 --> 01:23:25,481
- Four months.

2475
01:23:25,481 --> 01:23:26,938
- She'll be showing by then.

2476
01:23:26,938 --> 01:23:29,566
- Seems like a long time, doesn't it?

2477
01:23:29,566 --> 01:23:31,372
- I'm beginning to miss you already.

2478
01:23:31,372 --> 01:23:33,090
- [Mike] But I'm not gone, so.

2479
01:23:33,090 --> 01:23:35,364
- Honey I, I was wondering if.

2480
01:23:35,364 --> 01:23:37,344
- [Servo] If you heard
how the twins are doing.

2481
01:23:37,344 --> 01:23:39,376
- Well, if I could ask you to wait for me.

2482
01:23:39,376 --> 01:23:40,875
- [Crow] Right here, under this tree.

2483
01:23:40,875 --> 01:23:42,767
- I was hoping you'd ask me that.

2484
01:23:42,767 --> 01:23:46,767
- [Mike] I'll wait with
your best friend, Steve.

